                "description": "# Specific:\n\n\n# General:\nIn many cases, current data does not support the level of specificity that the full ontology allows, or the information is simply best expressed in human-readable form. For example, instead of a completely modeled set of parts with materials, many museum collection management systems allow only a single human-readable string for the \"medium\" or \"materials statement\".  Any time that there is a description of the resource, with or without qualification as to the type of description, then this branch can be used to record the descriptive text. See: https://linked.art/model/base/#statements-about-a-resource\n\n# Arches Note:\n\n\n* BranchId: la-statement\n* FieldId: \n",
